  "description": "The proposal seeks approval to temporarily demolish the rear boundary wall to gain essential site access during construction. The primary reason for this is to allow the movement of construction vehicles, machinery, and materials in and out of the site. Access from the rear of the property is necessary to prevent vehicles from entering through the front, which could disturb the neighbouring school. Our goal is to avoid this for safety and logistical reasons. A temporary access gate will be erected at the rear of the development site to safeguard the site and nearby residents.\n\nThe boundary wall will be carefully dismantled and fully reinstated to its original condition once the construction works are finished, ensuring it is rebuilt on a like-for-like basis, matching the existing materials, location, and design of the current wall. ",
